{
  "protocol": 1,
  "batch_id": "internode-logical-ag03-2x2-001",
  "mode": "dist",
  "supersedes": null,
  "requires": {
    "sm": 90,
    "gpus": 4,
    "env": "triton-dist"
  },
  "timeout_s": 600,
  "notes": [
    "Tutorial 03 of Triton-distributed 7908e4ea (inter-node all-gather): its kernels all_gather_push_1d_kernel and all_gather_push_2d_kernel, unchanged, on 64 bytes, 4 ranks. one_node/* is the control under triton-dist (one node of 4 ranks); logical_nodes/* runs 2 logical nodes of 2 ranks, where the 2D kernel reaches its receive-then-forward branch (lines 156-177 of the tutorial).",
    "Uses FOUR GPUs, by the user's decision of 2026-11-13 (documents/GpuExchangeProtocol.md, section 9): make two NVLink pairs visible, the two GPUs of one pair first, then the two of the other (CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=a,b,c,d with a-b one pair and c-d another), all four idle. Ranks 0 and 1 then run on the first pair and ranks 2 and 3 on the second, under both launchers; under logical_nodes/* each logical node holds one pair.",
    "Expected, judged on the development side only (experiments/interp_gpu/internode_logical/judge.py): every test ok; every rank returns the 64 input bytes.",
    "The two pairs are connected to each other over PCIe only. Whether NVSHMEM can map the memory of a GPU of the other pair is not known before this run: if it cannot, initialization ends with \"Peer GPU ... is not accessible\" and the test with runtime_error. That is a result, not a fault of the GPU side; a retry would end the same way.",
    "The harness runs the tutorial functions, not the tutorial program, and gives each signal tensor one word per rank, as in internode-logical-ag03-001. See harness.py and documents/GpuInterNodeRuns.md."
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "id": "one_node/push_1d",
      "frontend": "triton-dist",
      "entry": "experiments/interp_gpu/internode_logical/harness.py::all_gather",
      "launch": {
        "kernel": "push_1d"
      },
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "x",
          "dtype": "int8",
          "shape": [
            64
          ],
          "gen": {
            "class": "normal",
            "seed": 1
          },
          "sha256": "e7dbc37ca408aa79d667169e9a2bbf875e980a01428c6216fbd7ab4a17b5019f"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "topology",
          "dtype": "int32",
          "shape": [
            6
          ],
          "sentinel": "0x80000000"
        },
        {
          "name": "gathered",
          "dtype": "int8",
          "shape": [
            64
          ],
          "sentinel": "0x80"
        }
